surya: battery SOC from the power-on OCV and a coulomb counter

Only when the locally built ADT has /surya-battery (capacity and the 25 C
OCV-by-SOC column of the surya battery profile): start SOC from the QG's
S7_PON_OCV (only if it agrees with V - I*R now) through that table, then
the battery current sampled every second
is integrated; publish and log every 30 s; SMB5 termination sets 100%; a
failed read keeps the last values instead of the 100% fallback. Without the
node SweetBattery is unchanged for sweet.

Read-only charger diagnostics: APSD type, ICL setting/status, AICL, FCC;
the PM6150 RTC seconds at start (needs 0902).
Backlight: an AppleARMBacklight service (backlight-control = true), started
from SweetBattery when the local ADT has /backlight. iOS's "brightness"
(0..1024) drives the PM6150L WLED5 through sweet_spmi_write (0902): 0 turns
the module off, N sets level N*4095/1024 (min 42) as qcom-spmi-wled.c does.
Time: SweetPlatformExpert's clock hooks (0903) go to surya_time_* in
sweet_touch.c (0900) and IORTC is published; the 1 s timer calls
surya_time_tick until the saved time is applied.

Brightness across reboots: the last non-zero brightness iOS set is saved in
/private/var/db/surya-backlight 2 s after it changes; once the root is mounted
it is applied (unless iOS set one first) and published as the IODisplayParameters
"value" iOS fades from, instead of a fixed 512. The 1 s timer also drives the
notification LED (0900) with the last published charger state.

The "vibrator" service (SuryaVibrator, 22.10): iOS's FigVibrator falls back to
an IOKit vibrator found with IOServiceNameMatching("vibrator") and drives it
with IORegistryEntrySetCFProperties: {hertz_millisecs: [state, ms, ...],
repeat}, a state being {intensity: 16.16} or false, and a bare number 0 to
stop. setProperties logs what arrives and hands the pairs to surya_vib_play()
(0900).
